    {
      "id": "b8a5c84cb435175f5eb49fe6c887edfb826fc943",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 752742031,
          "type": null,
          "body": "It do what I expect just partly. It outputs to console even --debug-file is used. And I'm missing documentation about purpose of --capchild and who/how should use it.\n\nIf you run:\n\n`/run/extcap/randpktdump --extcap-interface=randpkt --type dns --count 10 --fifo=FILENAME --capture --debug`\n\nit works fine. But if you run:\n\n/run/extcap/randpktdump --extcap-interface=randpkt --type dns --count 10 --fifo=FILENAME --capture --debug --debug-file=/tmp/abc\n\nit works at first look OK. /tmp/abc contains what expected. But it does two strange things:\n1. It logs some messages to console even just file should be used\n2. Log messages on console are messy. With other extcaps it core dump when --debug-file is used. So it looks that there is some issue with memory management. But I'm not sure whether it is related to your patch or just exhibits something what was there already.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7791033,
            "username": "j.novak",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "j.novak@netsystem.cz",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b98b9c10d87ea9f383019b704e727c94ba6895dd3c46291d23e400738e1c6f1d?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/j.novak"
          },
